    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160616048?u=c67d934d3d5438fa90d22a59e3c49636cd31c75c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #25569.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2768044366\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25569\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25569/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25569\">#25569</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Set Safari support for the HTML global attribute autocapitalize to “yes”.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Evidence: <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/AppleApplications/Reference/SafariHTMLRef/Articles/Attributes.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40008058-SW1\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/AppleApplications/Reference/SafariHTMLRef/Articles/Attributes.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40008058-SW1</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28520",
            "title": "html.global_attributes.autocapitalize: Mark Safari as supported",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T16:59:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T16:58:54.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ssswdwads",
                "url": "https://github.com/ssswdwads"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From version 142 onwards, Chrome restricts <code class=\"notranslate\">pointerrawupdate</code> events (and associated event handlers) to secure contexts. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5151468306956288\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5151468306956288</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It has been this way in other browsers and the spec, and has been reported this way on MDN, for a long time. It also isn't a distinct feature. As a result, I've not added a separate data point for this — I've just added a note to the existing Chrome data point for the event to cover it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also stopped the equivalent Opera data from mirroring, and gave it a separate version number and equivalent note. I did this because I didn't want the note to be exactly the same under the Opera data.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28519",
            "title": "Chrome 142 restricts pointerrawupdate events to secure contexts",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T16:58:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T15:20:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118266?u=5a7fb2f3d1ecc7dcd73f43f4b478cb4938e6572c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 144 supported <code class=\"notranslate\">moveBefore</code>, alongside the <code class=\"notranslate\">connectedMoveCallback</code>. This updates the data to reflect the <code class=\"notranslate\">connectedMoveCallback</code> which was perhaps missed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3422725499\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27902\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27902/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27902\">#27902</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
