        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54687718?u=a1ad4b5e0600c9029222f99e5df2c7ef7ae19a59&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Hi <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hamishwillee/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hamishwillee\">@hamishwillee</a>,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As per your request on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3583703942\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41795\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41795/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41795\">mdn/content#41795</a>, I'm opening this PR to add the note about Safari's <code class=\"notranslate\">localhost</code> exception for <code class=\"notranslate\">Secure</code> cookies directly to the BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've added the note to the main <code class=\"notranslate\">Set-Cookie</code> support block for Safari, as <code class=\"notranslate\">Secure</code> isn't tracked as a separate sub-feature. Please let me know if this is the correct location!</p>\n<hr>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a BCD note to the <code class=\"notranslate\">Set-Cookie</code> header, clarifying that Safari does not support the <code class=\"notranslate\">localhost</code> exception for the <code class=\"notranslate\">Secure</code> attribute.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a data-only change to add a <code class=\"notranslate\">note</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Supporting information and related discussion:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Original WebKit bug report: <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=281149\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=281149</a></li>\n<li>This change follows the request from <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hamishwillee/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hamishwillee\">@hamishwillee</a> in the related <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn/content</code> PR (see below).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41366.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3474798100\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41366\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41366/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41366\">mdn/content#41366</a><br>\nAddresses discussion in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3583703942\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41795\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41795/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41795\">mdn/content#41795</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28461",
            "title": "Safari does not support `localhost` exception for `Secure` cookies",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-21T19:28:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-15T19:36:53.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Mattia-Rollo",
                "url": "https://github.com/Mattia-Rollo"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">…te() calls</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">javascript:</code> URLs are no longer allowed in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigation/navigate\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Navigation.navigate()</code></a> calls (see <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3292278858\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11533\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/11533/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11533\">whatwg/html#11533</a>), and I thought this should be mentioned in BCD, as the state of support for this change differs across browsers:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox implemented it in Fx144 (<a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1981104\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1981104</a>), but the Navigation API was only enabled in Nightly as of Fx146, so I didn't think a note was needed here. I tested this to verify.</li>\n<li>Chromium browsers still allow it (see <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/439994590\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/439994590</a> for the removal bug), so I thought a note was needed there, so say it is still allowed. I tested this in Chrome Canary, and yup, it still works.</li>\n<li>Safari has fixed it in preview (see <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=297650\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=297650</a>). I tested this to verify. I've not added any Safari data because the whole API says it is not supported in Safari. Obviously, this needs updating, but I think it is out of scope for this PR.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28440",
            "title": "Add note about javascript: URLs being disallowed in Navigation.naviga…",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-17T13:57:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-12T14:37:07.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45960703?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Google Chrome deprecated (Browsing) Topics API.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Google Chrome deprecated (Browsing) Topics API, so mark the following MDN features deprecated:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>document.browsingTopics()</li>\n<li>browsingtopics attribute on HTML &lt;iframe&gt;</li>\n<li>browsingTopics option in fetch()</li>\n<li>Sec-Browsing-Topics HTTP request header</li>\n<li>Observe-Browsing-Topics HTTP response header</li>\n<li>HTTP header Permissions-Policy directive browsing-topics</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Source:<br>\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/_R85yctz4Rs\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/_R85yctz4Rs</a></p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tracking MDN issue <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3603007045\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28417\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28417/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28417\">#28417</a>.</p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28418",
            "title": "Deprecate Google Privacy Sandbox (Browsing) Topics API",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-18T10:41:41.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-08T12:53:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bershanskiy",
                "url": "https://github.com/bershanskiy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 143 adds support for the WebGPU <a href=\"https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gpufeaturename-texture-component-swizzle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">texture-component-swizzle</code></a> feature, which, when enabled, allows usage of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUTexture/createView\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">createView()</code></a> method's <a href=\"https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gputextureviewdescriptor-swizzle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">swizzle</code></a> option that allows developers to perform color swizzles.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5110223547269120\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5110223547269120</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for both the feature and the option.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also took this opportunity to clean up the rest of the Chrome feature data, as a bunch of the entries weren't quite right (the Chrome Android data shouldn't mirror Chrome when Chrome is marked partial implementation and has a note, neither of which are relevant to CxA).</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28411",
            "title": "Chrome 143 WebGPU texture-component-swizzle feature",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-22T11:43:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-07T16:44:43.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unmarks Firefox as partial for <code class=\"notranslate\">::highlight</code> CSS Selector, and splits up the existing notes, adding bug links.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I challenge the following <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/tree/main/docs/data-guidelines#partial_implementation-general-usage-guidelines\">requirement for partial implementation</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The browser's support has a demonstrable negative impact on web developers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3586286163\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374\">#28374</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28375",
            "title": "Unmark Firefox as partial for `::highlight` CSS selector",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-12T17:49:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-04T12:12:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chromium browsers support <a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/protections/user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">User-Agent reduction</a>, which means that features such as the <code class=\"notranslate\">User-Agent</code> HTTP header provide less-specific information in an effort to reduce their effectiveness for fingerprinting/tracking.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds data points covering User-Agent reduction to relevant web platform features that I know to be affected by the change.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Compat data sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>From looking at <a href=\"https://blog.chromium.org/2021/09/user-agent-reduction-origin-trial-and-dates.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://blog.chromium.org/2021/09/user-agent-reduction-origin-trial-and-dates.html</a>, it looks like rollout of UA reduction to 100% of Chromium desktop users occurred in version 110, while the version was 113 for Chromium Android users. I asked <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/miketaylr/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/miketaylr\">@miketaylr</a> about this, and he confirmed it to be correct.</li>\n<li>From looking at <a href=\"https://www.chromium.org/updates/ua-reduction/#applicable-platforms\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.chromium.org/updates/ua-reduction/#applicable-platforms</a>, it looks like Android WebView should be <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another question for Mike: For all of these data points, I used <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/#user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/#user-agent</a> as the <code class=\"notranslate\">spec_url</code>. Are there better spec URLs we can point to for these individual features?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is part of the final set of privacy sandbox information to be added to MDN. Much of it is being removed, but this feature is stable and will be kept, so it should be added.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28275",
            "title": "Chrome 110 applies User-Agent reduction to Navigator properties + `User-Agent` header",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-07T14:33:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-23T15:21:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        }
    ]
}